+     "Reverse translation").  A regular in-tree symlink stores a guest
+     path already, so its target is left as is -- and, importantly,
+     dn-policy's own readlink() calls (symlink resolution, hardlink
+     bookkeeping) are on non-/proc host paths and must keep seeing the
+     raw target.  */
+  char dn_path[DN_PREFIX_MAX];
+  int dn_proc = 0;
